core=dict(status='usable',rationale='Representative formation and authority paths and their supporting persistence, membership, recovery and consumption boundaries are traced; detailed variants remain open, not claimed complete.',formation=dict(explanation='Peer.ProposeEntries enters leader handler, assigns current term and sequential index, updates self match, and broadcasts replication. Followers check previous term/index, reject mismatches, append a matching suffix and cap propagated commit. Leader counts remote and witness matches at majority position, excluding observers, and only advances by counting a current-term index. Acknowledgments retry rejected replication and successful commit is propagated. Engine exports updates, saves state/entries before dependent outbound responses, queues committed entries for RSM application and acknowledges processed state separately from applied state. RSM applies commands/session semantics and callbacks report completion.',behavior_ids=['B-formation','B-history','B-application'],fact_ids=['F-commit'],source_ids=['M-formation','M-term','M-read','M-engine','M-node','M-update','M-rsmapply']),context=dict(explanation='Ticks initiate campaigns only for eligible nonremoved full members and only after committed work is applied. Candidate increments term and self-votes; vote grants check saved vote and log freshness; known eligible responses elect a majority. Becoming leader resets replication progress, reconstructs pending configuration status and appends a no-op. Higher terms step down with a recent-leader vote-suppression exception; stale terms are discarded. CheckQuorum steps down when voters are inactive; transfer suppresses proposals and waits for target catch-up before TimeoutNow. Reset abandons prior votes, pending read confirmations and transfer but preserves committed history. Snapshot recovery restores membership; self removal steps down.',behavior_ids=['B-authority','B-membership','B-recovery'],fact_ids=['F-context'],source_ids=['M-transitions','M-term','M-peer','M-tick','M-transfer','M-checkquorum','M-members','M-restore']),connection=dict(explanation='Authority reset prevents counting prior-term progress, while the surviving committed log constrains election freshness and future replication. Applied membership defines voting support; single pending configuration and election blocking on unapplied commit connect application timing to quorum overlap. ReadIndex separately requires a current-term commit before asking voters to confirm authority. A matching heartbeat quorum releases queued read statuses; emitted readiness then needs a matching caller context and locally applied index. Pending confirmations are volatile and reset on authority changes; request completion is separately timed and correlated.',behavior_ids=['B-authority','B-membership','B-read-admit','B-read-confirm','B-read-consume'],fact_ids=['F-context','F-commit','F-readpending'],source_ids=['M-members','M-term','M-transitions','M-read','M-readqueue','M-confirm','M-batches']),core_gaps=[],open_details=['Remote ReadIndex response context differs from local release when one confirmation releases a prefix.','Snapshot storage/transport and asynchronous recovery variants need deeper reading.','Membership acceptance validation and in-flight support across configuration transitions remain open.'])
